# uv.lock is a byproduct of `uv build` / `uv venv`, which
# scripts/verify_packaging.py runs. This project's lock is
# requirements-research.lock.txt (see its header and the invariant check in
# scripts/check_invariants.py); two lockfiles at the root would be two
# answers to one question.
uv.lock

# Fresh-acquisition working data. Both are DERIVED and regenerable, and both
# grow every trading day:
#   - the raw bhavcopy ZIPs are a fetch cache; each row's provenance is the
#     sha256 recorded in the acquisition report, not the archive itself, and
#     ~200KB per session per day would bloat the history for no gain.
#   - research_data/current/ is rebuilt from the corpus on every acquisition.
#     The FROZEN research_data/*.parquet stays tracked: it is the hashed input
#     research_results/v1 was produced from.
artefacts/bhavcopy_raw/
research_data/current/
